# D365 Finance & SCM Unified Multi-Ledger Costing Engine Design

**Document Version:** 2.0  
**Analysis Date:** January 20, 2026  
**Prepared by:** Senior D365 Architect / GIA Expert / Cost Accounting Functional Consultant  
**Scope:** Distribution / Trading Company Scenario (generalized design)

---

## Design Philosophy: Native Integration, Not Add-On

> **Critical Design Decision:** The future-state costing engine is a **native capability within D365 Finance and Supply Chain Management**, not an external add-on. This represents a **merger of GIA concepts and Cost Accounting** into the core product, eliminating the current fragmentation and deployment complexity.

---

## Why Native Integration Matters

| Add-On Approach (Current GIA) | Native Integration (Proposed) |
|------------------------------|-------------------------------|
| Requires LCS add-in installation | Part of standard D365 deployment |
| Depends on Power Platform/Dataverse | Uses native D365 F&O infrastructure |
| Shadow subledger only (no GL posting) | Full GL integration with multi-book posting |
| Separate from Cost Accounting module | Unified with Cost Accounting capabilities |
| Async processing via external service | Synchronous or near-real-time processing |
| Additional licensing considerations | Included in Finance/SCM license |
| Limited partner expertise | Standard D365 implementation skills |

