# 1. Global Inventory Accounting – Key Concepts & Capabilities

## 1.1 Purpose & Scope

### What Problem GIA Solves

**Global Inventory Accounting (GIA)** is an add-in for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management that addresses a fundamental challenge for international organizations: **the need to report inventory value differently to different stakeholders** while maintaining a single operational truth.

| Business Driver | GIA Solution |
|-----------------|--------------|
| **Multi-standard compliance** | Same inventory transaction valued under IFRS, US GAAP, local GAAP, and management standards simultaneously |
| **Multi-currency consolidation** | Subsidiaries operate in local currency; group reporting in EUR/USD; GIA maintains parallel currency valuations |
| **Dual valuation requirements** | Statutory books may require weighted average; tax authority may accept standard cost; management wants full absorption—all from one transaction |
| **Audit trail across representations** | Single source transaction with traceable calculation to N different inventory values |

### How GIA Relates to Standard SCM Inventory Costing

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│            OPERATIONAL INVENTORY TRANSACTION                 │
│         (PO Receipt, SO Invoice, Transfer, etc.)            │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                           │
           ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
           ▼                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│  STANDARD SCM COSTING   │    │   GLOBAL INVENTORY          │
│                         │    │   ACCOUNTING (GIA)          │
│  • Posts to GL          │    │   • Shadow subledger only   │
│  • Single valuation     │    │   • N parallel valuations   │
│  • Single currency      │    │   • N currencies            │
│  • Book of record       │    │   • Reporting/analysis      │
└─────────────────────────┘    └─────────────────────────────┘
```

**Key architectural point:** GIA operates as a **shadow subledger**—it generates accounting entries but does NOT post to the General Ledger. Standard D365 inventory costing remains the book of record for GL purposes.

