## 1.3 Business Document Coverage & Processing Model

### Supported Business Documents

| Document Category | Specific Documents | Events Generated |
|-------------------|-------------------|------------------|
| **Purchase Order** | Product Receipt | Inventory inflow + cost capture |
| **Purchase Order** | Invoice | Cost adjustment (actual vs. accrued) |
| **Sales Order** | Packing Slip | Inventory outflow + revenue recognition prep |
| **Sales Order** | Invoice | COGS recognition |
| **Inventory Journals** | Movement | Internal transfer between dimensions |
| **Inventory Journals** | Adjustment | Quantity/value corrections |
| **Inventory Journals** | Counting | Physical count variances |
| **Inventory Journals** | Transfer | Movement between locations |
| **Transfer Order** | Shipment | Inventory in transit |
| **Transfer Order** | Receive | Arrival at destination |

### Event-Based Processing Architecture

GIA uses an **event-sourced architecture**:

```
Operational Transaction → Operational Event → GIA Event → GIA Measurements
                           (single source)    (N per ledger)  (cost entries)
```

#### Measurement Types

For each event, GIA generates two types of measurements:

| Measurement Type | Description | Examples |
|------------------|-------------|----------|
| **Operations Measurements** | Business document details in generic terms | Product quantity (in document UoM), extended price, discount, line charges |
| **Resource Accounting Measurements** | Inventory register impact in inventory UoM | Inventory quantity change, cost amount change |

#### Dimension Structure

Measurements are organized by dimensions:

| Dimension Category | Purpose | Examples |
|-------------------|---------|----------|
| **Duality** | Who participates in the economic event | Legal entity (primal), Vendor/Customer (dual) |
| **Dimension Type** | Categorization of dimensions | Cost object, Cost element, Subledger account |
| **Dimension Value** | Specific value within dimension | Product ID, Site ID, Account number |

### Asynchronous Processing

**Critical:** GIA processes documents **asynchronously** after they're posted in SCM. This means:
- No blocking of operational transactions
- Eventual consistency between SCM and GIA views
- No real-time error messages for GIA processing issues

