## 1.4 Multi-Ledger & Multi-Standard Accounting

### Multiple GIA Ledgers per Legal Entity

A single legal entity can have multiple GIA ledgers to support different reporting requirements:

| Ledger | Purpose | Configuration |
|--------|---------|---------------|
| **GAAP_USD** | US statutory reporting | Calendar: Fiscal, Currency: USD, Method: Avg |
| **IFRS_EUR** | International consolidation | Calendar: Fiscal, Currency: EUR, Method: Avg |
| **TAX_USD** | Tax compliance | Calendar: Tax, Currency: USD, Method: Standard |
| **MGMT_USD** | Management reporting | Calendar: Fiscal, Currency: USD, Method: Standard |

### Dual-Currency / Dual-Valuation Reporting

| Scenario | How GIA Addresses |
|----------|-------------------|
| **Dual currency** | Create two ledgers with different currencies; same Convention |
| **Dual valuation** | Create two ledgers with different Conventions (e.g., one Avg, one Standard) |
| **Currency + Valuation** | Create N ledgers with appropriate currency/Convention combinations |

### Processing Flow

```
Single Operational Event
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    GIA EVENT PROCESSOR                           │
│                                                                  │
│  For each active GIA Ledger associated with this Legal Entity:  │
│    1. Apply Convention policies                                  │
│    2. Determine cost elements and values                         │
│    3. Convert to ledger currency using specified FX rate        │
│    4. Generate GIA measurements and subledger entries           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │
    ┌─────┴─────┬─────────────┬─────────────┐
    ▼           ▼             ▼             ▼
┌────────┐ ┌────────┐    ┌────────┐    ┌────────┐
│GAAP USD│ │IFRS EUR│    │TAX USD │    │MGMT USD│
└────────┘ └────────┘    └────────┘    └────────┘
```

