## 2.4 Security & UX

### Cost Control Units

A **Cost Control Unit** defines the cost structure for security and reporting:
- Which cost object dimension hierarchy to use
- Controls how costs flow hierarchically
- Foundation for access rights configuration

### Access Rights for Cost Object Controllers

| Role | Capabilities |
|------|--------------|
| **Cost Accounting Manager** | Full access to all configuration and data |
| **Cost Accountant** | Configure and run overhead calculations |
| **Cost Accountant Clerk** | View and process cost data |
| **Cost Object Controller** | View cost data for assigned cost objects only |

**Row-level security:** Access list hierarchies control which cost objects each user can see, enforced across:
- Cost Control Workspace (client)
- Cost Control Workspace (mobile)
- Power BI visualizations

### Cost Control Workspace

The **Cost Control Workspace** is the primary user interface for managers:

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Report configurations** | Multiple report layouts per cost accounting ledger |
| **Period selection** | View current period, previous period, YTD |
| **Budget comparison** | Actual vs. original budget vs. revised budget |
| **Variance thresholds** | Highlight when variances exceed thresholds |
| **Drill-through** | Navigate from summary to cost entry details |

**Workspace configuration options:**
- Columns to display (Fixed, Variable, Total, Unclassified)
- Fiscal periods to include
- Budget versions for comparison
- Variance threshold highlighting

### Power BI Integration

| Component | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Entity Store** | Cost accounting data published for BI |
| **Content Pack** | Pre-built Power BI reports |
| **Row-Level Security** | Access list hierarchy paired with Power BI RLS |

