### Why Cost Accounting Feels Complex

| Complexity Factor | Description | Impact |
|-------------------|-------------|--------|
| **Separate from GL** | Parallel data structure to General Ledger | Dual maintenance, reconciliation burden |
| **Many policy types** | Four policy types (Behavior, Distribution, Allocation, Rollup) with subtle differences | Confusion about which to use when |
| **Dimension redundancy** | Cost elements ≈ Main accounts; Cost objects ≈ Financial dimensions | "Why am I defining this twice?" |
| **Hierarchy complexity** | Two hierarchy types (Categorization, Classification) with different rules | Non-intuitive structure |
| **Formula learning curve** | Formula allocation bases require technical understanding | Not accessible to typical cost accountants |
| **Security setup** | Access list hierarchies separate from standard D365 security | Additional configuration layer |
| **Data connector setup** | Mapping source data to Cost Accounting structures | Technical implementation burden |
| **Multi-step overhead calculation** | Four sequential steps with specific ordering | Process complexity |
| **Versioning overhead** | Each calculation creates versions; managing versions is additional work | Operational overhead |

### Customer Adoption Barriers

| Barrier | Manifestation |
|---------|---------------|
| **Expertise requirement** | Only specialized consultants can implement |
