# 7. Key Trade-offs, Risks, and Open Questions

## 7.1 Key Trade-offs

| Trade-off | Choice Made | Rationale | Risk if Wrong |
|-----------|-------------|-----------|---------------|
| **Native vs. GIA add-on foundation** | Build natively into D365 | Eliminates add-on friction; enables GL posting; simplifies deployment | Larger engineering effort than extending GIA |
| **Merge GIA + Cost Accounting** | Single unified capability | One mental model; one configuration surface; clearer value prop | Transition complexity for existing users |
| **Template-based vs. fully configurable** | Templates + overrides | Faster adoption; covers 80% of scenarios | Advanced users may feel constrained |
| **Any-book GL posting vs. single primary** | Any book can post (via posting layers) | True multi-GAAP GL; no shadow-only limitation | More complex reconciliation; posting layer training |
| **Inherit from GL vs. parallel configuration** | Inherit with overrides | Less duplication; easier maintenance | Couples costing to GL structure |
| **Pre-built statistical measures vs. custom** | Auto-import + limited custom | Reduces configuration burden | May miss specialized use cases |
| **Standard D365 security vs. custom hierarchy** | Standard D365 | Simpler; leverages existing investment | Less granular cost object access |
| **Batch vs. real-time processing** | Both (configurable per book) | Flexibility for different volumes | Complexity in processing modes |

## 7.2 Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|------------|--------|------------|
| **Engineering effort larger than expected** | Medium | High | Phase delivery; start with valuation layer (Layer 1) |
| **Existing GIA customers reluctant to migrate** | Medium | Medium | Provide migration tools; parallel-run capability; clear value messaging |
| **Posting layers not well understood** | Medium | Medium | Training; good defaults; limit to common layer patterns |
| **Customers want full Cost Accounting** | Medium | Medium | Offer "advanced mode" that exposes more capability |
| **Template library insufficient** | Medium | Medium | Plan for template customization and community templates |
| **Statistical measure auto-import too limited** | Medium | Low | Provide fallback manual import option |
| **Performance at scale** | Medium | High | Prototype with large transaction volumes early |
| **Migration from current GIA/Cost Accounting** | Medium | Medium | Provide migration tools and parallel-run capability |
| **Dependency on D365 platform changes** | Low | High | Align with D365 platform roadmap; use stable APIs |

